Wyoming
By virtue of and pursuant to the authority vested in me
as President of the United States and by the act of June 25,
1910, ch. 421, 36 Stat. 847, as amended by the act of August
24, 1912, ch. 369, 37 Stat. 497, it is ordered that all lands
owned or controlled by the United States in the followingdescribed areas, .comprising 19,939.78 acres in Teton County,
Wyoming, be, and they are hereby, subject to valid existing
rights, included in and reserved as a part of the Elk Refuge,
established by Executive Order No. 2177 of April 21, 1915:
